1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hi. In this video, we'll use Burp to manipulate WebSocket handshakes.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:16,920
A WebSocket handshake is a HTTP message that establishes a WebSocket connection.

3
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:21,860
You can often access additional attack surface by manipulating these messages.

4
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:27,720
We'll demonstrate how you can clone, modify, and resend WebSocket handshakes in Burp Repeater.

5
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:32,120
If you'd like to follow along, you can use the lab, Manipulating WebSocket Messages to

6
00:00:32,120 --> 00:00:37,740
Exploit Vulnerabilities from our Web Security Academy.

7
00:00:37,740 --> 00:00:44,480
Once the lab has launched, browse around the target application to map the attack surface.

8
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:49,120
Now switch to the Proxy, WebSocket's History tab.

9
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:53,600
This tab displays a table of any WebSocket messages Burps browser has exchanged with the target

10
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,360
host.

11
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:59,600
Right click on one of the messages and select Send to Repeater.

12
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,940
We can now switch to the Repeater tab and see that Burp has opened a new WebSockets tab.

13
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:09,240
Click on the Edit icon to view a list of WebSocket connections that have been used in your current

14
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:11,180
Burp session.

15
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,420
Select the connection you want to base your new connection on and click Clone.

16
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:22,100
If required, amend the host, port, and use HTTPS settings.

17
00:01:22,100 --> 00:01:26,280
Then in the Request panel, you can now amend the message.

18
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:29,620
There are a wide range of exploits you could perform here depending on the application's

19
00:01:29,620 --> 00:01:32,740
logic and how it uses WebSockets.

20
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:38,220
For example, you could add an XForwarded4 header to spoof your IP address, enabling you to get

21
00:01:38,220 --> 00:01:41,520
around restrictions on your actual IP.

22
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:45,620
Click Connect to create the modified connection.

23
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:50,940
Click on the Edit icon to view the list of all WebSocket connections.

24
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:55,680
Select the new connection from the list and click Attach.

25
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:59,460
Repeater will now use the new connection for all messages sent from the Open tab.

26
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:08,860
Select the new connection.

27
00:02:08,860 --> 00:02:12,180
Select the new connection.

28
00:02:12,180 --> 00:02:16,140
Select the new connection.

29
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:18,140
Select the new connection.

30
00:02:18,140 --> 00:02:20,140
Select the new connection.

31
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,140
Select the new connection.

32
